+      <p class="lede">A Lite-plan style comparison using <code>missing-offer.html</code> (score 44 in this run) beside <code>strong.html</code> (score 100). Fixture evidence only; not a customer result.</p>
+      <p class="meta">Published 2026-09-13 · Companion markdown retained in S01 W202 evidence</p>
+      <div class="callout"><strong>Why this matters:</strong> Offer price, currency, and availability presence failures are common template bugs. Lite (up to five public URLs) can compare pages and attach a retest checklist after payment is actually connected.</div>
+      <section>
+        <h2>What we observed on the weak fixture</h2>
+        <p>The missing-offer fixture fails or warns on Offer-related field coverage. The strong fixture passes the same bounded checks. A cross-page comparison highlights the gap without claiming the weak storefront cannot sell products.</p>
